  "outline": [
    {
      "beat": "lingers",
      "brief": "Late in the computer lab (Kiran is a computer science researcher): open plan, desks in two rows by the window set back to back, low dividers between neighbouring desks that only screen the desk tops, printers, a big table on the far side; cosy and warmly lit, everyone else gone. Kiran at her corner desk. Ranulf (Ran), her childhood friend, back in town for a week after fifteen years away and leaving tomorrow, comes back in for a scarf he says he forgot (an excuse to stay), and sits at the desk beside hers. He is easy and direct; he flirts with her."
    },
    {
      "beat": "spark",
      "brief": "Kiran answers with dry teasing: she says the opposite of what she feels (that she is glad he's leaving), and he reads it correctly and grins; he knows her too well."
    },
    {
      "beat": "note",
      "brief": "Kiran steps out to the kitchen to make tea (she plans to come straight back). Ran, alone, writes a short initialled note ('Roof. Eleven. Like before. There's something I should have said. —R') and leaves it on her desk, then goes up to the roof."
    },
    {
      "beat": "find",
      "brief": "Kiran comes back with her tea to an empty lab and the note on her keyboard. She picks it up and reads it. 'Like before': as children they met on the garage roof between their houses at eleven at night."
    },
    {
      "beat": "doubt",
      "brief": "She reads it as nostalgia, a goodbye for old times' sake, and tells herself not to want more from it. She goes up anyway, because it is his last night."
    },
    {
      "beat": "climb",
      "brief": "Kiran climbs the stairs to the roof, the note in her pocket, the city below."
    },
    {
      "beat": "confess",
      "brief": "On the roof Ran tells her the note meant what it said, not old times: what he should have said fifteen years ago, before his family moved, is that he liked her then and he likes her now."
    },
    {
      "beat": "negotiate",
      "brief": "Ran asks, out loud and plainly, whether he can kiss her. Kiran says yes; he says yes too (consent on both sides, explicit). Kiran wants it."
    },
    {
      "beat": "kiss",
      "brief": "The kiss: Kiran kisses Ran. Close on what she notices."
    }
  ]
